id: templates/node
title: "templates node"
kind: mental-model-node
status: active-mixed
updated: 2026-08-27

purpose: >
  Hold reusable .yawn shapes that people and agents can copy without learning
  the whole ontology.

holds:
  - basic template
  - observation template
  - observation-question-art template
  - orientation shape template
  - feedback template
  - full template
  - decision template
  - relationship template
  - proof template
  - proof receipt template
  - agent handoff template
  - access record template
  - backup record template
  - next-move record template
  - open-question template
  - arena template
  - asynchronous turn template
  - structural routing proposal template
  - structural change receipt template
  - objective holon template
  - orientation_inquiry projection fields over an independent orientation_map

receives:
  - repeated movement patterns
  - proof and boundary constraints
  - agent handoff needs
  - question packet mappings

produces:
  - copyable forms
  - consistent records
  - intake-driven draft frames
  - lower cognitive load
  - versioned state, desire, optional-target, transition, proof, and update shapes

canonical_rule: >
  New templates use attributed state snapshots, first-class desires, optional
  scoped targets, and separate transition intent/result. Legacy current,
  possible, possible_kind, and measurement fields are compatibility aliases.
  Draft 0.2 templates keep arena, one primary parent, typed lateral relations,
  asynchronous turns, routing proposals, and authorized structural receipts
  distinct. Objective Holon 0.1 also keeps candidate, ratification, Yawn, bot,
  and activation distinct. No current human template is marketed as the
  complete .yawn schema. orientation_inquiry presentation fields reference an
  independent orientation_map View and never become semantic state themselves.

questions:
  - what shape should this yawn use
  - which question packet can fill this template
  - what fields are required
  - what can be deleted

links:
  - start/node.yawn
  - questions/node.yawn
